// VerifyClaimsAgainstSource's literal-quote grounding exists specifically
// to catch the one failure mode that step can introduce: the model
// citing a quote that isn't really in the source (hallucination). A
// candidate typing "7" directly into a "Total Years of Experience" field
// has not been through any inference step at all - there is nothing to
// extract, and therefore nothing that could have been hallucinated. The
// value IS the evidence, by construction. Running the exact same,
// real-money Anthropic call on data that is already unambiguous
// structured input would be pure redundant cost for zero uncertainty
// -reduction benefit - the same reasoning System Review item 43 already
// established for CANDOR-04's JD re-extraction (see
// CANDOR-04-Build-Log.md §27-28): don't pay an LLM to resolve
// uncertainty that doesn't exist.
