// same `fields`/`employment_history`/`portfolio_or_work_sample`/
// `verification_summary` contract CANDOR-04's own IntakeCandidateRecord
// already expects and falls back to) so CANDOR-04, CANDOR-05, CANDOR-07,
// and CANDOR-08 all need ZERO changes to accept this new source - this
// is a new intake PATH into the same pipeline, not a new pipeline.
//
// `evidence_verified: true` for a directly-submitted field is not a
// weaker or faked verification - it correctly reports the one specific
// thing that flag has ever meant anywhere in this codebase ("this value
// did not arise from an LLM inventing a quote"), and that claim is
// trivially and honestly true here: there is no LLM step on this path
// at all. It says nothing about whether the candidate told the truth -
// exactly like every other evidence_verified flag in this project, which
// has never verified factual accuracy, only extraction fidelity.
//
// HONEST LIMITATION, stated plainly: quantified_accomplishments and
// notable_unquantified_claims are deliberately left empty - this form
// does not collect freeform accomplishment narrative (classifying free
// text into "quantified" vs "unquantified" claims without an LLM would
// mean reinventing a second, cruder extraction path, which this
// adapter's whole design exists to avoid). Evidence Confidence's
// denominator (verification_summary) is therefore smaller for an
// application-form candidate than a typical resume-derived one (the 8
// scalar fields only, never the 11-15 a resume with several
// accomplishments produces) - a real, structural difference from the
// file-upload path's own reporting depth, not a gamed or inflated score.
// employment_history holds at most ONE entry (the form asks only for the
// candidate's single most recent/most relevant role, not a full career
// history), so career_trajectory's "progression" sub-component (which
